\ float — port of pyperformance bm_float, a trig/sqrt-heavy point benchmark.
\ For each i in [0,n): a point (sin i, cos i · 3, sin²i / 2); normalize each to
\ unit length; then componentwise-maximize across all points.
\
\ The reference builds n Point objects; telic keeps the three coordinates
\ in flat nx1 vectors (no per-point boxing), so the inner loops are pure
\ raw-double reads and writes — exactly the shape the compiler's vf*/vvf*
\ fusion targets. The whole benchmark is repeated REPEAT times for a stable
\ measurement; the reported result is the final maximized point.

100000.0 constant points
60.0 constant repeats

variable xs  variable ys  variable zs
variable maxx variable maxy variable maxz

\ i-times over head-receiving quotations, not do/loop: the do form measured
\ slower here — the loop-refill path under i-times undercuts the do form's
\ bookkeeping on these bodies.
: build-points
  [: i |
     i fsin to sxi
     xs sxi i !e drop
     ys  i fcos 3.0 f*  i  !e drop
     zs  sxi sxi f* 2.0 f/  i  !e drop
  :] points i-times ;

: normalize-points
  [: i |
     xs i @e to xi  ys i @e to yi  zs i @e to zi
     xi xi f* yi yi f* f+ zi zi f* f+ fsqrt to length
     xs  xi length f/  i  !e drop
     ys  yi length f/  i  !e drop
     zs  zi length f/  i  !e drop
  :] points i-times ;

: maximize-points ^maxx ^maxy ^maxz |
  xs 0 @e to maxx  ys 0 @e to maxy  zs 0 @e to maxz
  [: i |
     xs i @e to xi  xi maxx >= if xi to maxx then
     ys i @e to xi  xi maxy >= if xi to maxy then
     zs i @e to xi  xi maxz >= if xi to maxz then
  :] points i-times ;

: float-once ^xs ^ys ^zs |
  points 1 0-matrix to xs
  points 1 0-matrix to ys
  points 1 0-matrix to zs
  build-points
  normalize-points
  maximize-points ;

: float-run
  now to t0
  ' float-once repeats times
  now t0 - to t0
  "result: " . [ maxx maxy maxz ] frame>json . cr
  "elapsed: " . t0 . " s" . cr ;

float-run
bye
